---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Disclosure" description="How Nonprofit Software Guide is funded, and how that affects (and doesn't affect) what we recommend.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Disclosure' }]} />
    <article class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <h1>Disclosure</h1>

      <p>
        Nonprofit Software Guide is a free, independent publication. Some of the
        links on this site are affiliate links. If you click one and later start
        a paid plan with that vendor, the vendor pays this site a commission. You
        pay nothing extra, and in some cases you pay less: where a vendor offers
        a reader discount through our link, we note it next to the link.
      </p>

      <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Links that route through this site's tracking (our <code>/go/</code> links) may earn a commission.</li>
        <li>Affiliate relationships never decide a recommendation. Tools that pay us
        nothing are recommended by name throughout the site where they are the right
        answer, including Zeffy for zero-fee processing, Little Green Light and Eleo
        on the strictest budgets, and free library access to Candid for grant
        research.</li>
        <li>Where a category is better served by hiring a consultant than by buying
        software, the stack pages say so and carry no product link at all.</li>
        <li>We do not accept payment for placement, rankings, or reviews. No vendor sees content before it publishes.</li>
        <li>Prices and terms come from vendor pricing pages and are checked on a regular schedule. Vendors change pricing; always confirm current terms on the vendor's site before buying.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our relationship with vendors</h2>
      <p>
        We want the software companies we cover to succeed. Good fundraising
        software makes nonprofits more effective, and the best way to evaluate
        any tool on this site is to take the vendor up on a demo or free trial
        and test it against your own data. When we recommend booking a demo,
        that is the recommendation: see it yourself before you decide.
      </p>

      <p>
        This disclosure is made in accordance with the FTC's guidelines on
        endorsements and testimonials. Questions about it can be sent through
        the contact information on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
